  "conclusion": "Supplying the true initial slot does not unlock generalizable three-swap tracking. The final classifier metrics and CE are exactly unchanged by a wrong oracle state or batch-shuffled swap clips. The trained updater therefore exposes no task-usable dependence on either input and collapses toward a class-prior solution. The next isolating experiment should directly classify the swapped cup pair from each 10-frame segment, without recurrent state, to test whether the frozen patch embedding plus K64 pooling preserves the transition evidence at all."
